$$\begin{equation*}
C=\int_{0}^{r} 2 \pi r w d r=\frac{1}{2} \beta r . \tag{6}
\end{equation*}$$


It appears, therefore, that the magnetic force at a given point
 due to a current arranged in cylindrical strata, whose common
 axis is the axis of $z$, depends only on the total strength of the
